  "description": "The original benchmark for titanium road race bikes, built with our legendary Superform SL tubeset for ultimate all-around comfort and performance. Litespeed introduced the Ultimate in 1987, and when it was released, it was our “ultimate” road bike. It’s been refined and perfected over decades and remains the benchmark that all other titanium bikes are measured against. Frame weight: 1,295 grams (size medium) Superform SL 3AL/2.5V titanium tubeset Aeroform design with bladed seatstays and airfoil-shaped downtube PF30 bottom bracket - threaded T47 upgrade available Universal Derailleur Hanger (UDH) Maximum tire size: 35mm* Proudly handcrafted in Chattanooga, TN, using globally sourced premium materials *Varies based on tire brand, tread, and wheel combination.",
